  "metadata": {
    "alignment": "standard",
    "description": "eugr's (Eugene Rakhmatulin) spark-vllm-docker recipe for Qwen's official Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-FP8 (block-wise FP8, Apache-2.0; checkpoint revision 95a723d0) served by vLLM on two Sparks. Runs eugr's published vllm-node image (nightly-20260929, digest pinned; its build-metadata records spark-vllm-docker 42f62e34, vLLM 0.30.1rc1.dev336+gaf5b4857e and FlashInfer 4a638133) with upstream's launch: VLLM_MARLIN_USE_ATOMIC_ADD=1, FlashInfer attention, FP8 KV cache, fastsafetensors loading, prefix caching, qwen3 reasoning and qwen3_xml tool parsing, eugr's fix-qwen3.6-chat-template mod (baked into the image at build time; the chat template it installs is selected with --chat-template), 262,144-token context, 16,384 batched tokens and memory utilisation 0.8 (upstream defaults); scheduler sequence capacity is left to vLLM as upstream does not set it. This is upstream's recipe as written (tensor parallel 2); the Controller runs it as native multi-node vLLM (eugr's default no-Ray cluster mode, instead of --distributed-executor-backend ray). No upstream performance claims are recorded. Upstream repository MIT. Physical Spark acceptance is pending. Version 1.0.1 (2026-09-30) adds a single `speculation` selector (autoregressive default or native Qwen3.6 MTP) and a `modality` selector (multimodal default or zero-limit language-model-only). On the pinned vLLM release that mode disables multimodal inputs but retains the Qwen3.5 vision tower, so it is not a VRAM-reduction switch. The native MTP choice uses the MTP head already in the pinned FP8 checkpoint and the pinned vLLM parser; it adds no model files, image changes, or runtime downloads. Sources: https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-FP8/tree/95a723d08a9490559dae23d0cff1d9466213d989 and https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/af5b4857e/vllm/engine/arg_utils.py.",
